    // ── privacy ──
    priv_title: 'Privacy — Fabro', priv_h1: 'Privacy',
    priv_lead: 'Fabro is built so that your conversations, files and models stay on your computer. Here is exactly what stays, and what goes online.',
    priv_stays_h: 'What stays on your computer',
    priv_stays: '<li>Your conversations, projects, memories and settings.</li><li>The files you open, attach or let the agent work on.</li><li>The AI models and everything they generate — text, images, audio.</li><li>What you say in voice mode: speech recognition and voices run locally.</li><li>Fabro has no account and no analytics. We do not know who you are or how you use it.</li>',
    priv_goes_h: 'What goes online — only when needed',
    priv_goes: '<li><b>Downloads</b> you ask for: models from Hugging Face; the llama.cpp engine, image engine and tools from GitHub; Python packages for voice and search.</li><li><b>Updates</b>: Fabro checks GitHub Releases for a new version and for engine updates.</li><li><b>Web search and browsing</b>, when you or the agent use them. Searches go through a private SearXNG instance running on your computer, which queries search engines without an account.</li><li><b>Online providers</b> (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google…), only if you connect them yourself — then your messages go to that provider, under its own terms.</li>',
    priv_crash_h: 'Crash reports are opt-in',
    priv_crash: 'Off by default. If you turn on “Offer to send crash reports”, Fabro keeps problem reports on your computer and, after a crash, offers to open a pre-filled GitHub issue that you can read and edit before sending. Home-folder paths are masked. Nothing is sent automatically.',
    priv_site_h: 'This website',
    priv_site: 'No cookies, no trackers, no analytics. Your theme and language choice are kept in your browser only. The download button and the changelog ask GitHub\'s public API for the latest release.',
    priv_contact: 'Questions? Open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/lulualdn/fabro-ai/issues">GitHub</a>.',
