    legal_title: 'Legal notice — Fabro', legal_h1: 'Legal notice',
    legal_pub_h: 'Publisher', legal_pub: 'Fabro and this website are published by <b>UFStudios</b>. Contact: through <a href="https://github.com/lulualdn/fabro-ai/issues">GitHub issues</a>.',
    legal_host_h: 'Hosting', legal_host: 'This website is hosted by Netlify, Inc., 512 2nd Street, Suite 200, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. Downloads are served by GitHub, Inc.',
    legal_use_h: 'Use of the software', legal_use: 'Fabro is provided free of charge, “as is”, without warranty. AI models can be wrong: check important answers. Models you download are subject to their own licences, shown on their Hugging Face pages.',
    legal_tm_h: 'Trademarks', legal_tm: 'Fabro and the propeller logo belong to UFStudios. Other names (Windows, macOS, Linux, model and provider names) belong to their owners and are used only to describe compatibility.',
    legal_oss_h: 'Third-party software', legal_oss: 'Fabro is built on open-source software. Thank you to their authors.',
    legal_lic: 'Licence',
    any_b4_h: 'Your models, streamed to your pocket',
    any_b4_p: 'Ask from the phone: your computer’s models answer, word by word. On the same Wi-Fi the phone connects directly; elsewhere a relay puts them in touch — it only ever sees encrypted messages.',
    any_b5_h: 'Works offline',
    any_b5_p: 'Conversations live on the phone too and sync both ways on their own. Write while the computer is off: the message waits and goes as soon as it’s back. A small model can even answer on the phone itself (WebGPU) — and you can try it without any computer or account.',
    any_b6_h: 'Voice, photos, notifications',
    any_b6_p: 'Talk to Fabro with the phone’s microphone — your computer’s voices answer — send a photo to your vision models, open the documents and pages it made, and get a notification when an answer or an agent task is ready.',
    any_open: 'Open Fabro Anywhere',
    priv_any_h: 'Fabro Anywhere (phone)',
    priv_any: '<li>The phone and the computer pair by reading a code on your screen; they share keys that never leave them. Every message is <b>end-to-end encrypted</b>.</li><li>To find each other, both connect to public relays (MQTT: EMQX, HiveMQ, Mosquitto) or your own. Relays only see encrypted messages, store nothing, and are used as a fallback only when a direct connection (WebRTC, with Google’s STUN server to find a path) isn’t possible.</li><li>Notifications go through your phone’s push service (Google, Apple or Mozilla), encrypted so it can’t read them.</li><li>The optional phone model is downloaded from Hugging Face and its runtime from jsDelivr; then it runs on the phone.</li>',
